=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully operational. Every component relevant to the reported symptom was tested directly and found to be working correctly. DNS is authoritative and correct: the BIND server at 10.200.0.2 holds the zone "local" with the record `web0 A 10.200.0.3`, and an explicit nslookup from host_1_1_1_1 targeting that server resolves web0.local → 10.200.0.3 successfully. The web server (web_server_0) is alive: Apache 2.4.62 is listening on 0.0.0.0:80 with no firewall rules in place, and it responds HTTP 200 with the expected content ("Welcome to Web Server 0") when queried locally. End-to-end reachability from host_1_1_1_1 is confirmed: ICMP pings to 10.200.0.3 achieve 0% loss, and a verbose curl from host_1_1_1_1 to http://web0.local completed in under 5 ms returning HTTP 200 OK with the correct body — a result independently corroborated by Apache's access log, which shows the exact request arriving from 10.1.1.2 and being served with status 200. The multi-area OSPF topology (area 0 backbone with router_core_1 and router_core_2 as ABRs connecting area 1 distribution switches) is fully converged: all three OSPF adjacencies on router_core_1 are in Full state and every routing table carries complete inter-area prefixes. The user's report of the page "spinning and never appearing" does not correspond to any reproducible fault in the current lab state. No corrective action is needed; the portal is reachable and serving normally.
=== END ===